WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
Type sine of one hundred and
fifty degrees into a calculator.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.210
It says nought point five.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.090
Now press inverse sine, to undo it.

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.690
You'd expect one hundred and fifty back.

5
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.170
But the screen shows a different angle.

6
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.370
Why doesn't inverse sine undo sine here?

7
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.550
Is the calculator just rounding?

8
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.370
In this mission, you'll
meet three new functions,

9
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.880
secant, cosecant and cotangent:
the reciprocals of cos,

10
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.550
sine and tan.

11
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.960
You'll sketch their graphs, and
derive two new Pythagorean identities.

12
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.510
And you'll use the inverse trig functions:

13
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.890
arcsine, arccosine and arctangent.

14
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:44.570
Your mission: explain why inverse sine of
sine one hundred and fifty degrees isn't

15
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.210
one hundred and fifty degrees.
